From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 12:16:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] accel/ane: say when H16_LOAD accepts a second H16 program

The H16_LOAD documentation still says a firmware boot accepts one H16
program and refuses a second LOAD even after the first program closed.
Since "accel/ane: run linked H16 programs and load them one after
another" the session refuses a LOAD only while another program is still
loaded and accepts it once that program's file closed
(ane_h16_session_load()), and the program KUnit test loads a second
program after the first closed. Describe that rule in the uapi header and
in the H17 switch test comment. No code change.

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5.5
---
 drivers/accel/ane/ane_h16_program_test.c | 4 ++--
 include/uapi/drm/ane_accel.h             | 7 ++++---
 2 files changed, 6 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/accel/ane/ane_h16_program_test.c b/drivers/accel/ane/ane_h16_program_test.c
index 905ee53029..bb1bfe8990 100644
--- a/drivers/accel/ane/ane_h16_program_test.c
+++ b/drivers/accel/ane/ane_h16_program_test.c
@@ -1700,8 +1700,8 @@ static void program_h17_mobilenet_test(struct kunit *test)
 /*
  * An H17 session switches between programs: a second LOAD succeeds, and
  * every EXECUTE that follows a different program, a LOAD or a CREATE is
- * queued. H16 keeps one program lifetime, and a program built for the other
- * engine is refused before any traffic.
+ * queued. H16 holds one loaded program at a time, and a program built for
+ * the other engine is refused before any traffic.
  */
 static void program_h17_switch_test(struct kunit *test)
 {
diff --git a/include/uapi/drm/ane_accel.h b/include/uapi/drm/ane_accel.h
index 30d2ae73b8..74c05249b9 100644
--- a/include/uapi/drm/ane_accel.h
+++ b/include/uapi/drm/ane_accel.h
@@ -307,9 +307,10 @@ struct drm_ane_h16_section {
  * mapping, then loads the program and creates its process. The program
  * belongs to this file and is unloaded when the file closes. The HWX must
  * be compiled for the engine that GET_CAPS reports. On H17 a firmware boot
- * accepts any number of programs, one per file. On H16 a firmware boot
- * accepts one program: a second H16_LOAD fails with -EBUSY, also after the
- * first program closed, and a reboot starts a new firmware boot.
+ * accepts any number of programs, one per file. On H16 one program is
+ * loaded at a time: a second H16_LOAD, on this file or another, fails with
+ * -EBUSY while a program is still loaded, and is accepted once the file
+ * that loaded it closed.
  */
 struct drm_ane_h16_load {
 	__u64 hwx_ptr;
